title: The Unitary Power Decree
view-if: chancellor_party == "Royalist" and rubicon_mini_time == 2
new-page: true
tags: event
max-visits: 1
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/reichstag.jpg";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}

= The Unitary Power Decree

As the Assembly gets back to business once again, the bill on debate is not one of no-confidence, but rather an "Unitary Power Decree" proposed by [+ royalist_chancellor +] and the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>. With Staal's blessing, the cabinet believes that certain elements of the constitution will have to suspended in order to crush the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> and the Banners. 

However, this is not something the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] can easily swallow...

- @hitler
- @hitler_2

@hitler
title: The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] votes in favor.
view-if: (unionist_in_gov_mini and pro_republic < 30) or far_right_coalition >= 50

[? if not concord_formed: [+ unionist_leader +]?][? if concord_formed: [+ concord_formed +]?] is personally assured significant constitutional safeguards by Staal, though he fails to extract a written commitment from [+ chancellor +]. It proves meaningless—[+ chancellor +] never intended to honor them.

Gallax has promised a campaign of revenge against the <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformists</span>, and the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> have already spilled much blood on the streets. In his published manifesto, he promises a campaign of <span style="color: #7e0000;">**unspeakable**</span> <span style="color: #3f0000;">**horror**</span> against all who would stand for the republic, and endless wars to force the realms back under the Crown—a crusade that would set all of Athar ablaze.

What are we to do now?

- @fight: We will fight on the streets to prevent Gallax from taking power.
- @give_up: We will vote against the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> in the Assembly.

@fight

Do we realize that this means civil war, against the full force of the state?

- @civil_war: Yes.
- @give_up: We are not ready for war. Instead, we will vote against the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> in the Assembly.

@give_up

Speeches are made. Votes are held. Bullets fly in the streets. Some <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformists</span> are killed or jailed. Others flee the country. What can votes even do at this juncture?

The Assembly is burned, ostensibly by a foreign <span style="color: #700000;">collectivist</span>. In the wake, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> pass decrees giving them unlimited power. They, combined with the [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>?][? if dnf_formed: <span style="color: #003755;">**CNF**</span>?], will win a majority at the next elections.

the Commonwealth is lost.

- @game_over: Game over.

@hitler_2
title: The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] votes against!
view-if: (not unionist_in_gov_mini or pro_republic >= 30) and far_right_coalition < 50
on-arrival: rubicon_mini = 0; rubicon_mini_leave = 1;

[? if not concord_formed: [+ unionist_leader +]?][? if concord_formed: [+ concord_formed +]?] is personally assured significant constitutional safeguards by Staal, though he fails to extract a written commitment from [+ chancellor +]. [? if not concord_formed: [+ unionist_leader +]?][? if concord_formed: [+ concord_formed +]?] is able to see through these lies, and whips the party's parliamentary delegation to vote against the Unitary Power Decree. 

Staal regards this development as a betrayal, yet his options are limited. President DuFour remains the true deciding factor. He now views the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]’s refusal to support [+ chancellor +] has only deepened his impatience. Disillusioned, DuFour no longer considers [+ chancellor +]’s ambition to lead as a parliamentary chancellor to be credible.

- @hitler_3

@hitler_3
title: [+ chancellor +] refuses to resign!

In an act of defiance to President DuFour, Chancellor [+ chancellor +] has simply refused to acknowledge the president's power to dismiss the incumbent chancellor. The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> mobilize on the streets, and things could get bloody.

What are we to do now?

- @fight: We will fight on the streets to prevent Gallax from retaining power.
- @give_up_2: We will trust in the president's abilities.

@give_up_2
go-to: give_up_3 if loyalist_force < 50; give_up_4 if loyalist_force >= 50

The President may be on our side, but the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> can simply intimidate their way around him.

@give_up_3
on-arrival: {!
Q.next_election_month = Q.month + 3;
Q.next_election_time = Q.time + 3;
if (Q.next_election_month > 12) {
    Q.next_election_month -= 12;
    Q.next_election_year = Q.year + 1;
} else {
    Q.next_election_year = Q.year;
}

Q.pro_republic += 15;

Q.commons_royalist -= 6;
Q.disfavored_royalist -= 6;
Q.commons_collectivist += 3;
Q.disfavored_collectivist += 3;
Q.commons_marcher += 3;
Q.disfavored_marcher += 3;

Q.loyalist_strength *= 0.8;

Q.old_chancellor = Q.chancellor;

Q.chancellor = "Askew";
Q.chancellor_party = "Unionist";

Q.foreign_minister_party = "Gold";
if (Q.lvp_formed) Q.foreign_minister_party = "LVP";
Q.interior_minister_party = "Unionist";
Q.justice_minister_party = "I";
Q.labor_minister_party = "Unionist";
Q.army_minister_party = "I";
Q.economic_minister_party = Q.ddp_name;
if (Q.lvp_formed) Q.economic_minister_party = "LVP";
Q.finance_minister_party = "Gold";
if (Q.lvp_formed) Q.finance_minister_party = "LVP";
Q.agriculture_minister_party = "Unionist";

Q.gold_left += 4;
Q.ddp_left += 2;
Q.lvp_left += 4;
Q.bourgeois_cooperation += 3;
Q.liberal_cooperation += 5;

Q.rubicon_mini = 0;
Q.rubicon_mini_leave = 1;

Q.unionist_in_gov_mini = 0;
!}

The Commonwealth Army has placed more trust in [+ president +] than in Chancellor [+ old_chancellor +], and under this influence, [+ old_chancellor +] was forced to accept his defeat. His removal, along with the replacement of many <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> cabinet ministers, has stopped the Commonwealth's slippery slope into dictatorship.

Edmund Askew of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] is selected as interim chancellor. The next elections are set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year + 2365 +].

@give_up_4

Unfortunately, President DuFour is forced to concede defeat after a war game orchestrated by Staal reveals that the Commonwealth Army and Police cannot prevail in a civil war against the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> and other paramilitary forces.

Reduced to little more than a figurehead, DuFour remains in office—signing off on every decree, fully aware that any resistance would plunge his beloved nation into civil war.

the Commonwealth is lost.

- @game_over: Game over.